      "Language": "jpn",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Recently, the multidetector computed tomography (CT) is available to measure quantitative analysis of coronary vascular calcification (coronary calcification score [CACscore]). Vascular calcification is recognized not only in the end stage of atherosclerosis but also in the early stage of atherosclerosis. Recent data suggested that bone- related factors are closely related to coronary artery disease and vascular calcification. In this review, we discuss for regulatory mechanisms of vascular calcification."},
